    {
      "claim": "The committed C02-family C01 rung was marched off the frozen wall-spacing ladder.",
      "evidence": "artifacts/.../S1_tip_first/m2_deformation_20260830/C01_template/lhs100_seed42_083/prepare_manifest.json records level_settings.s0_frac=6.1e-06 for candidate_c01 but s0_fraction_override=3.6e-06, giving s0=4.731044780752643e-06 - the same absolute wall spacing as the C03 template (4.73106217171235e-06). resolution.py S6_FIRST_CELL_FRACTION['candidate_c01'] is 6.1e-06.",
      "id": "F1",
      "impact": "C01 and C03 share a wall spacing, so the A C01/C02/C03 sequence is not a coupled grid+wall-spacing refinement ladder. Any grid-convergence or refinement claim built on the C01 rung is not supported by the artifacts as marched. A concurrent session has since added C01 screens for B/C/E to m2_proven_route_family_20260830.json (geometry C at C01 is below the 0.10 production floor at qmin 0.0840); those rows inherit the same off-ladder wall spacing and should be re-read once F1 is closed.",
      "severity": "HIGH",
      "status": "open - requires either a re-march of C01 at 6.1e-06 or an explicit governed statement that C01 is a fixed-wall-spacing rung"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The deformation route does not preserve the wall-spacing policy across geometries.",
      "evidence": "The affine chord/span map scales wall-normal spacing with the geometry. B/C/E C02 use the geometry-A template (first layer min 3.334e-06 m, median 1.159e-05 m) with scales 0.81-0.95 and land at min 2.713e-06..2.754e-06 m, median 9.45e-06..9.59e-06 m - about 18 percent below the template.",
      "id": "F2",
      "impact": "Realized first-cell height, and therefore y+, differs per geometry in the atlas. The deformation report already marks first-layer spacing 'diagnostic_pending_production_yplus_validation'; this must be closed before the CFD canary, not after.",
      "severity": "MEDIUM",
      "status": "open"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Interface evidence is complete and unchanged by deformation, but the pairing is heuristic.",
